      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The University of the Pacific is a private Methodist-affiliated university with its main campus in Stockton, California, and graduate campuses in San Francisco and Sacramento. Founded in 1851, it is the oldest chartered University in California.</p><p>Over 6000 students have enrolled at the University of the Pacific annually, with around 470 international students making up the student body.</p><p>The Student Health Center offers medical and mental health services, including counseling and wellness programs. Multiple research institutes and centers are available on campus, including the Pacific McGeorge Global Center for Business and Development, the Pacific Center for Environmental Studies, and the Brubeck Institute. Similarly, arts programs are supported by various arts facilities, including the Raymond Great Hall, the Faye Spanos Concert Hall, and the Jeannette Powell Art Center. The Stockton campus also has a tall rock-climbing tower.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The University of the Pacific provides housing options for its Stockton campus that cater to individual preferences. The four residence halls on campus each include double and triple occupancy rooms, shared lounges, community bathrooms, study rooms, and more. Multiple suite-style buildings suit students seeking to enjoy kitchenettes and common areas.</p><p>Some students opt for apartments on campus instead, featuring a range of occupancy rooms, a shared living room, a bathroom, and a kitchen. This arrangement is fully furnished, and all bills are included in the price. Substance-free housing, wellness housing, and gender-neutral housing are all accommodation options available from the University.</p>",
      "image": null,
